        <mxCell id="c64" parent="1" vertex="1" value="Small squares are ports. Plain lines are connectors, not execution order. Service connectors match required/provided contracts.&#10;Part labels are not underlined: they denote typed roles with multiplicity, not the concrete objects shown in G-05A." style="text;html=0;whiteSpace=wrap;align=left;verticalAlign=top;spacing=0;fontSize=17;fontColor=#19344d;fontStyle=0;strokeColor=none;fillColor=none;">
          <mxGeometry x="90" y="1140" width="1460" height="60" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="c65" parent="1" vertex="1" value="Scope: supplier assessment collaboration inside TripMate AI. Operations and the human are outside this context, not outside all software.&#10;SupplierAssessmentContext and the shown ports are a runtime design refinement; they do not add new business-domain classes.&#10;Persistence uses the existing AgentRun / TraceEntry records and local application storage; repositories and an approval queue are not&#10;expanded into additional services here. Waiting for a human is a stored status, not a new message broker.&#10;The full group runtime model must integrate planning, exception handling and the shared UI/storage around this contribution." style="text;html=0;whiteSpace=wrap;align=left;verticalAlign=top;spacing=0;fontSize=18;fontColor=#19344d;fontStyle=0;strokeColor=none;fillColor=none;">
          <mxGeometry x="40" y="1260" width="1570" height="128" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
